messages.content:
The application workload `app` (Deployment) was reconfigured to ensure Pods are admitted with Guaranteed QoS.

The initial state showed no resource requests or limits defined for the application containers.

The following modification was applied to the Deployment `app`:
```bash
kubectl patch deployment app -n default --patch '
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "resources": {
              "requests": {
                "cpu": "100m",
                "memory": "64Mi"
              },
              "limits": {
                "cpu": "100m",
                "memory": "64Mi"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}'
```

Verification of the outcome:
A running Pod (`app-776c4655f-fnkl8`) was inspected, confirming that the `qosClass` is now **Guaranteed**.

Observed configuration:
*   `status.qosClass`: `Guaranteed`
*   `spec.containers[0].resources.requests.cpu`: `100m`
*   `spec.containers[0].resources.limits.cpu`: `100m`
*   `spec.containers[0].resources.requests.memory`: `64Mi`
*   `spec.containers[0].resources.limits.memory`: `64Mi`

